      "message": "fix(fixtures): judge each picked stock face on its mate plane\n\nThe stock-mate check compared only the boxes of the carried and the\nfollowed stock. A cylinder stock whose cap is mated to a vertical stop\nre-fits upright with the same box, so the cap stayed perpendicular to\nthe stop and the locate was accepted.\n\nstock_lands (now in fixture_locate_land.rs) keeps the box check and then\njudges each picked stock face where the mates put it: the followed stock\nmust hold facets that face the same way (NORMAL_TOL) on that plane\n(LEN_TOL_MM), covering the face's area (FACE_AREA_REL_TOL) and each of\nits facet centres. A picked stock vertex must be a corner of the\nfollowed stock. A failure is refused in LocatePart::new, by name.\n\nPinned by fixture_locate_stock_cylinder (the review repro refused, the\ncap on the floor located at the right height with the collision check\nreading the landed stock, a quarter-turned cap judged by the face check).\n\nFixes #2173\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
